3. SIZE / LIPOPHILICITY CONFOUND — RAW docking vs LIGAND EFFICIENCY
==============================================================================
  Docking score = PfDHFR affinity (kcal/mol, more negative = stronger binding).  n = 609.
  A negative r means BIGGER / GREASIER molecules get 'better' (more negative) scores.

  docking vs MW    Pearson r = -0.102 (weak), Spearman rho = -0.167 (weak)
      -> ok: no strong MW dependence (|r| <= 0.5).
  docking vs logP  Pearson r = -0.274 (weak), Spearman rho = -0.293 (weak)
      -> ok: no strong logP dependence (|r| <= 0.5).

  Now the SAME descriptors vs LIGAND EFFICIENCY (LE = docking / heavy_atoms):
  The fix works if LE's |r| vs MW drops toward 0 — size no longer buys score.
  LE vs MW         Pearson r = +0.857 (STRONG), Spearman rho = +0.866 (STRONG)   [raw |r|=0.10 -> LE |r|=0.86]
      -> SIZE OVER-SWING: LE now tracks MW STRONGLY in the opposite sense (it favours smaller molecules); watch the known-drug LE percentile and LE-top size for fragment bias.
  LE vs logP       Pearson r = +0.191 (weak), Spearman rho = +0.197 (weak)   [raw |r|=0.27 -> LE |r|=0.19]
      -> logP confound now weak (|r| <= 0.3).

